        {
          "id": 5134,
          "text": "Calendly integration FAQs",
          "highlight": false,
          "color": "#475467",
          "bold": false
        }
      ],
      "faqList": [
        {
          "id": 2715,
          "header": "What does the Calendly integration do?",
          "body": "It adds a scheduler field to your form so respondents can book a meeting on your Calendly while filling out the form — no separate booking step.",
          "body_markdown": "",
          "list": []
        },
        {
          "id": 2714,
          "header": "How do I add Calendly to a form?",
          "body": "Click Add Elements → Appointment Scheduler (under Date & Time), choose Calendly under Schedule With, paste your Calendly link, and publish.",
          "body_markdown": "",
          "list": []
        },
        {
          "id": 2717,
          "header": "Can the booking reuse their name and email?",
          "body": "Yes — enable autofill in the field properties and the respondent's name and email carry into the Calendly booking.",
          "body_markdown": "",
          "list": []
        },
        {
          "id": 2716,
          "header": "What kinds of meetings can people book?",
          "body": "Anything your Calendly offers — demos, consultations, interviews, support calls — controlled by the appointment link you paste in.",
          "body_markdown": "",
          "list": []
        },
        {
          "id": 2718,
          "header": "What is Formester?",
          "body": "Formester is an online form builder for creating forms, surveys, and quizzes with a drag-and-drop editor or AI. It connects with the tools your team already uses — Google Sheets, Slack, HubSpot, Zapier, and more — so your form data flows wherever you need it.",
          "body_markdown": "",
          "list": []
        }
      ]
    },
